## 13. Frontend Security Considerations

Although most security is handled by the backend, the frontend contributes through:

* Sending JWT tokens only for admin API requests
* Avoiding exposure of sensitive backend logic
* Using controlled form inputs
* Avoiding hardcoded sensitive credentials
* Handling API errors safely

Admin tokens are stored in localStorage for development convenience. For production, further security improvements may be considered.

